    {
      "id": "el43",
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#868e96",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 721762279,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 502922617,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1010,
      "y": 975,
      "width": 381.59999999999997,
      "height": 75.0,
      "text": "OpenTelemetry spans would give timing per hop.\nNeeds instrumentation plus ~15 lines to carry\ntraceparent across Kafka, since auto-instrumentation\nstops at the producer.  request_id correlation covers\ncausality today, but not where the time went.",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontFamily": 3,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "OpenTelemetry spans would give timing per hop.\nNeeds instrumentation plus ~15 lines to carry\ntraceparent across Kafka, since auto-instrumentation\nstops at the producer.  request_id correlation covers\ncausality today, but not where the time went.",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true
    },
    {
      "id": "el44",
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#f08c00",
      "backgroundColor": "#fff9db",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": {
        "type": 3
      },
      "seed": 2120395275,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 253207297,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "type": "rectangle",
      "x": 1480,
      "y": 150,
      "width": 820,
      "height": 487.25
    },
    {
      "id": "el45",
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#f08c00",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 937195260,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 1234510746,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1500,
      "y": 168,
      "width": 512.72,
      "height": 21.25,
      "text": "THE METRICS THAT MATTER  \u2014  instrument what fails SILENTLY",
      "fontSize": 17,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "THE METRICS THAT MATTER  \u2014  instrument what fails SILENTLY",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true
    },
    {
      "id": "el46",
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 555512016,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 1063497604,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1500,
      "y": 203,
      "width": 483.59999999999997,
      "height": 406.25,
      "text": "A failed index is visible: the document is not searchable and\nsomeone complains.  These three are not, which is the whole\nreason they are instrumented.\n\n  outbox_unpublished_depth\n      growing  ->  the relay is stuck.  documents are being\n      accepted and 202'd, and nothing will ever index them.\n\n  kafka_consumer_lag\n      growing  ->  the indexer is behind and the search index\n      is drifting from the source of truth.\n\n  documents_by_status{status=\"FAILED\"}\n      a backlog nobody is draining.\n\n  DLQ depth\n      alert at > 0, not > 100.  one dead-lettered DELETE means\n      a document the user deleted is still findable  \u2014  a\n      privacy incident wearing a queue metric's clothing.\n\nAnd one that guards the latency budget:\n\n  cache hit ratio\n      the budget assumes 60-70%.  below that, Elasticsearch\n      takes traffic the cache was supposed to absorb.",
      "fontSize": 13,
      "fontFamily": 3,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "A failed index is visible: the document is not searchable and\nsomeone complains.  These three are not, which is the whole\nreason they are instrumented.\n\n  outbox_unpublished_depth\n      growing  ->  the relay is stuck.  documents are being\n      accepted and 202'd, and nothing will ever index them.\n\n  kafka_consumer_lag\n      growing  ->  the indexer is behind and the search index\n      is drifting from the source of truth.\n\n  documents_by_status{status=\"FAILED\"}\n      a backlog nobody is draining.\n\n  DLQ depth\n      alert at > 0, not > 100.  one dead-lettered DELETE means\n      a document the user deleted is still findable  \u2014  a\n      privacy incident wearing a queue metric's clothing.\n\nAnd one that guards the latency budget:\n\n  cache hit ratio\n      the budget assumes 60-70%.  below that, Elasticsearch\n      takes traffic the cache was supposed to absorb.",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true
    },
    {
      "id": "el47",
